  {"Record(s)": "1-1(06/25/2025):Acknowledged the feedback shared on the call, and documented the discussion in meeting summary.\\n1-2(06/25/2025):Provided a timeline of 06/24 to share the findings and action plan.\\n1-3(08/05/2025):August 5th, 2025: Internal connect between SDU and CE to provide status on the progress and explore possible solutions to improve Certs tasks quality.\\n2-1(06/25/2025):CE was part of the 6/18 monthly meeting with the client.\\n2-2(06/25/2025):Acknowledged the SDU action plan on 06/19\\n2-3(08/05/2025):August 5th, 2025: SDU and CE discussed following topics in internal connect:\\n1. Update on status of action plan\\n2. Update on feedbacks since last meeting with the client - 3 feedbacks received but none are client found errors \\n3. Proposal to move the Certificate task under the Cert COE\\n2-4(09/26/2025):09/22: Sharon escalated feedback about 2 NOC cases. \\nRCA Outcome:\\n- Both the cases were processed as per the procedure\\n- RCA shared with the client, CE and CE Director\\n- Meeting with CE to discuss NOC feedback and share some of the scenarios related to Sovereign response on 09/25.\\n2-5(01/21/2026):Issue downgraded to Yellow.\\n\\n• Consistent reduction in number of feedbacks observed between November and January:\\no November: 30 feedbacks\\no December: Reduced to 17 feedbacks\\no January (up to Jan 21, 2026): Further reduced to 8 feedbacks\\n\\n• Improvement in quality and reduction in client found errors observed between November and January:\\no November: 3 client found errors reported and overall quality at 99.97%\\no December: 2 client found errors reported and overall quality at 99.98%\\no January (up to Jan 21st, 2026): No client found errors reported\\n4-1(06/25/2025):RCA shared with the client on 06/24. Client acknowledge the RCA and requested to include the error details in June Monthly Insight Report\\n4-2(07/17/2025):Based on the RCA, following actions were implemented:\\n1. 100% audits for Certificate tasks\\n2. For all feedbacks categorized as 'Procedure Update', procedures have been revised and this has been communicated to the client. \\n3. Increased internal audits to 25% from June 23rd, 2025 to July 18th, 2025 for Policy Checking tasks.\\n4. A retrospective audit covering an additional 25% of policies completed for Policy Checking tasks processed during the four-week period from May 26th, 2025, to June 20th, 2025. Corrections have been completed for all errors identified during this audit.\\n4-3(07/29/2025):Additional actions were implemented:\\n1. Team Leaders should conduct 100% audits for received and sent emails to client.\\n2. 100% audits for Policy Checking tasks.\\n3. 25% audits for all other tasks.\\n4. Complete procedure validation.\\n4-4(08/14/2025):August 7th, 2025: \\n1. The client has agreed to align the team with Certs COE. SDU will work on the transition plan and share with CE.\\n2. The client is also evaluating a new tool named - Certificate Hero.\\n4-5(08/29/2025):August 29th, 2025:\\n1. Certificates COE team has received credentials for 3 team members on 8/25.\\n5-1(07/17/2025):All feedbacks were updated in the June 2025 MIR.\\n5-10(08/22/2025):August 20th, 2025 - Monthly meeting with the client:\\nBelow topics were discussed during this meeting:\\n- Transition status: Transition is complete and the China team will be offboarded by end of August 2025.\\n- Provided update on July Volume, SLA and Quality\\n- Discussion on feedbacks and questions related to Certificate task\\n5-11(08/22/2025):August 21st, 2025:\\n- Certificate COE team introduced to clients\\n- 'On-Demand Certificate Workflow Checklist - Standard Template' shared with the client. Certificates team will share the updated checklist with the client in August 25th week.\\n5-12(08/22/2025):Update as of 8/22:\\n- Proposal to place account with Certificates COE approved; team introduced to client\\n- Target: 100% volume transition by the Week of September 22, 2025\\n- Shared On-Demand Certificate Workflow Checklist – Standard Template; updated checklist to be shared by 8/25 \\n- Transition complete; China team to be offboarded by end of August 2025\\n- 100% audits continue for Policy Checking & Certificate tasks \\n- Total errors: 6\\n5-13(08/28/2025):August 26th, 2025: Week 4 - August 18th to August 22nd - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 5 feedbacks received, 2 Client Found Errors, 1 Procedure Updates,1 Client Found Error - No and 1 Others (IT)\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 42 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-14(09/08/2025):September 2nd, 2025: Week 5 - August 25th to August 29nd - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 5 feedbacks received, 1 Client Found Errors, 3 Process Clarification,1 Procedure Update/New Workflow\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 47 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-15(09/15/2025):September 9th, 2025: Week 6 - September 1st to September 5th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 7 feedbacks received, 1 Client Found Errors, 1 Process Clarification, 1 Others(IT, Tracking Log) and 4 Procedure Update/New Workflow\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 78 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-16(09/17/2025):September 17th, 2025: Week 7 - September 8th to September 12th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Total 7 feedbacks received, all are  Process Clarification.\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 71 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-17(09/17/2025):September 16th, 2025: Weekly meeting with the Maddie:\\nBelow topics were discussed during this meeting:\\n- 2 feedback clarification provided\\n- 6 question required clarification discussed\\n- Confirmation on current workflow process and adjustment required details are discussed\\n5-18(09/25/2025):September 15th, 2025: Week 8 - September 15th to September 19th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 7 feedbacks received, 1 Client Found Errors, 5 Process Clarification and 1 Procedure Update/New Workflow\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 72 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-19(09/25/2025):September 23th, 2025: Weekly meeting with the Maddie- Below topic was discussed during this meeting:\\nFeedback Review on identifying the Endorsement document\\n5-2(07/17/2025):BGL team shared status update of quality, feedbacks received and analysis findings with the client on 07/16/2025 monthly meeting.\\n5-20(09/26/2025):09/11: \\n- Certs Center transition status update shared on 9/10\\n- Certs COE takes over completely by Sept 15th\\n5-21(10/10/2025):September 30th, 2025: Week 9 - September 22nd to September 26th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 7 feedbacks received, 1 Client Found Errors and 6 Process Clarification\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 64 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-22(10/10/2025):September 30th, 2025: Weekly meeting with the Maddie- Below topic was discussed during this meeting:\\n- Master Account\\n- Rewrite and Reissue\\n- Follow Up Policy\\n- Travelers Click Bond Renewals account\\n- Anderson Law Group LLC\\n5-23(10/10/2025):October 8th, 2025: Week 10 - September 29th to October 3rd - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 1 feedbacks received, 1 Process Clarification\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 41 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-24(10/10/2025):October 1st, 2025: Weekly meeting with the Maddie- Below topic was discussed during this meeting:\\n- Underlying Policy\\n- Clarification on Premium Discount and Endorsement Payroll\\n5-25(10/23/2025):October 14th, 2025: Week 11 - October 06th to October 10th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 5 feedbacks received, 5 are Process Clarification\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 67 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-26(10/23/2025):October 23th, 2025: Week 12 - October 13th to October 17th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 4 feedbacks are received \\n- 100% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 50% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 62 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-27(11/07/2025):October 28th, 2025: Week 13 - October 20th to October 24th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 2 feedbacks are received \\n- 100% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 25% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 49 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-28(11/07/2025):November 4th, 2025: Week 14 - October 27th to October 31st - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 3 feedbacks are received \\n- 100% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 25% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 61 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-29(11/07/2025):November 4th, 2025: Weekly meeting with the Maddie- Below topic was discussed during this meeting:\\n- Account Division List Update\\n- Feedback on requested for quote\\n- Follow up pending requests\\n- Master Account\\n5-3(08/01/2025):July 30th, 2025: SDU along with Sydney Alvarez - Client Executive, and Taira Mandy - Director, Client Development, met Sovereign team to provide an update on the account and action plan. Below topics were covered in this meeting:\\n1. Transition Status and Performance Snapshot\\n2. Feedback Overview and Action Plan\\n\\nDetails on Feedback Overview and Action Plan:\\n- 43 feedbacks received between June 12th and July 29th; 23 are procedure updates, 13 are client reported errors, and rest 7 are feedbacks of other categories which are not errors.\\n- Policy Checking and Certificates are main contributors of feedback and will continue to remain a focal area for the team \\n- Action plan includes increased audit % for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks, 100% validation of questions for Certs with support of Certs COE, creation of email templates to standardize the questions.\\n5-30(11/13/2025):November 11th, 2025: Weekly Report to Sovereign on 11/10/2025\\n- Tiffany provided feedback for 8 pending Certs cases in the queue\\n- Certs team will work on the RCA and share findings with Tiffany\\n5-31(11/13/2025):November 11th, 2025: In CE Quarterly connect with Sovereign, the Client raised below concerns:\\n1. Policy Checking backlog:\\n- SDU team evaluated the pending cases in the queue and provided below details to CE\\n- 348 cases pending for Policy Checking, and all pending cases are well within the turnaround time\\n- Team provided the timelines by which all these cases will be completed\\n2. Additional billed FTEs budgeted:\\n- With current workload there is no need for additional billed FTEs in the account\\n3. Certs - Client feels that 25 Certs completion by 2 billed FTEs is lower than what their team could achieve\\n-   AHT of Sovereign Certs is over 30 mins wherein Certs standard AHT is 12 mins. \\n- Certs team will conduct time motion study and share the details\\n4. Certs Questions - Question rate around 40%. Sharon mentioned if we can't get certs questions down within the next 60 days, they are going to pull certs work back in house. \\n- October question rate is at 37% and Nov week 1 is at 43%.\\n- October was increased due to Clarifications going up to Carrier\\n- The analysis is already presented to Tiffany and the team is already working with TIffany to reduce the number of referrals\\n5-32(11/14/2025):November 11th, 2025: Week 15 - November 3rd to November 07th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 6 feedbacks are received \\n- 100% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 15% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 71 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-33(12/01/2025):November 19, 2025: Week 16 - November 10th to November 14th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 15 feedbacks are received \\n- 68% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 15% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 48 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-34(12/01/2025):November 25, 2025: Week 17 - November 17th to November 21st - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 6 feedbacks are received \\n- 60% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 15% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 56 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-35(12/01/2025):November 22th, 2025 - Monthly meeting with the client:\\nBelow topics were discussed during this meeting:\\n- Provided update on October Volume, SLA and Quality\\n- Policy Checking Updates\\n- Discussion on feedbacks and questions related to Certificate task\\n5-36(12/12/2025):December 2, 2025: Week 18 - November 14th to November 28th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 2 feedbacks are received \\n- 63% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 15% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 10 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-37(12/12/2025):December 11, 2025: Week 19 - December 01st to December 05th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 1 feedbacks are received \\n- 65% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 25% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 10 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-38(12/16/2025):December 16, 2025: Week 20 - December 08th to December 12th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 5 feedbacks are received \\n- 65% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 33% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 8 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-39(12/26/2025):December 23, 2025: Week 21 - December 15th to December 19th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 5 feedbacks are received \\n- 48% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 20% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 8 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-4(08/01/2025):July 31st, 2025: CE shared following communication with the client: We would like to extend an invoice credit for the inconvenience caused. Please see the below amounts to be credited:\\nJuly - $1,500\\nAugust - $1,500\\n5-40(12/26/2025):December 17th, 2025 - Monthly meeting with the client:\\nBelow topics were discussed during this meeting:\\n- Provided update on  November Volume, SLA and Quality\\n- Policy Checking Updates\\n- Discussion on feedbacks and questions related to Certificate task\\n- During the meeting, Sharon and Tiffany expressed satisfaction with the reduction in referrals and raised no concerns regarding the Certs Center team’s performance. \\n5-41(12/30/2025):December 19th, 2025 - Follow-up meeting with Certs team\\n- Reiterated their positive feedback and showed interest in transitioning from the FTE model to the Certs Center model.\\n5-42(01/09/2026):December 30, 2025: Week 22 - December 22nd to December 26th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 4 feedbacks are received \\n- 44% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 15% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 4 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-43(01/09/2026):January 6, 2026: Week 23 - December 29th to January 2nd - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 2 feedbacks are received \\n- 58% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 15% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 3 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-44(01/16/2026):January 13, 2026: Week 24 - January 5th to January 9th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- 2 feedbacks are received \\n- 8% audits conducted for Certificate tasks\\n- 10% audits conducted for Policy Checking task.\\n- 10 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-45(01/16/2026):January 13th, 2026 - Monthly meeting with the Maddie on Policy Checking:\\nBelow topics were discussed during this meeting:\\n- Insurance Board Package Policies\\n- Master Spreadsheet notification\\n- Policy Checked version missing\\n5-5(08/08/2025):August 5th, 2025: Week 1 - July 28th to August 2nd - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of the 7 feedbacks received, 3 are Procedure Updates, 3 Client Found Errors, and 1 feedback was related to MFA.\\n- 100% audits conducted for Policy Checking and Certificates tasks.\\n- 36 questions posted and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.  \\n5-6(08/14/2025):August 12th, 2025: Week 2 - August 4th to August 8th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 7 feedbacks received, 4 are process clarification, 1 Client Found Error, 1 Procedure Updates and 1 feedback related IT.\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 57 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-7(08/14/2025):August 12th, 2025 - Align the team with Certs COE:\\n- Transition plan shared with the client on August 12th, 2025\\n- Proposed transition duration is 5 weeks\\n- Aim to complete the 100% volume transition by September 15th, 2025\\n5-8(08/22/2025):August 19th, 2025: Week 3 - August 11th to August 15th - action plan progress shared with client:\\n- Out of 11 feedbacks received, 6 are process clarifications, 2 Client Found Errors, 1 Procedure Updates and 1 was not an error.\\n- 100% audits are conducted for Policy Checking and Certificate tasks.\\n- 41 questions were raised and all were reviewed by Certs COE team.\\n5-9(08/22/2025):August 19th, 2025 - Align the team with Certs COE:\\n- Plan has been approved by the clients\\n- Revised transition plan shared with CE\\n- Aim to complete the 100% volume transition by September 22nd, 2025 week\\n6-1(02/05/2026):• Consistent reduction in number of feedbacks observed between November and January:\\no November: 30 feedbacks\\no December: Reduced to 17 feedbacks\\no January: Further reduced to 15 feedbacks\\n\\n• Improvement in quality and reduction in client found errors observed between November and January:\\no November: 3 client found errors reported and overall quality at 99.97%\\no December: 2 client found errors reported and overall quality at 99.98%\\no January: No client found errors reported and quality at 100% \\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Sovereign Insurance Group - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "SOVEBGL", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Aven Charles", "Supervisor": "Shruthik Manju", "Teamleader": "Chetan Kutal", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Client complains about other quality issues", "Detailed Description": "During our monthly meeting on 6/18, Sharon Maslowsky, SVP Operations at Sovereign Insurance Group, shared feedback regarding the quality of our work. The recent feedback on 6/23 from CE is based on the questions, transition and the cyber event, and they are considering the terminating the services.\\n\\nAnalysis and findings:\\nBetween 6/12 and 6/20, we received 10 feedbacks, which have been validated and categorized as follows:\\n• Procedure Updates – 5\\n• Clerical Errors – 3\\n• Tracking Log Improvement – 1\\n• Follow-up Email – 1\\n\\nProcedure Updates:\\n• 3 updates have been included in the procedure and shared with the client.\\n• 1 update related to the Certs task is under progress by the China team.\\n• We are seeking clarification from the client on the remaining 1 update.\\n\\nClerical Errors: Sharing the details in the attachment. \\n\\nTracking Log Improvement - A brief of this feedback is provided below:\\n• A shared Excel tracking log used by multiple team members which is saved in Sovereign shared drive crashed due to its size and the high number of users.\\n• With the help of Client IT support, the file successfully recovered. However, upon access, the file appeared as 'Read Only'. The team reported this behavior to Client IT, explaining that the file is shared and updated collaboratively by multiple users.\\nActions implemented: We have split the log by task to reduce file size and manage simultaneous user access.\\n\\nFollow-up Email:\\nThis was a follow-up on task completion, and details of feedback is provided below:\\n• The team was working on two separate requests, each with different event dates, and handled by two different processors.\\n• Clients response on 6/17 applied to both. However, this response was shared only with Processor 1. Processor 2 followed up with client on 6/18.\\n• As the task was completed within SLA, no further action was required.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2026, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "1. Reduction in feedback observed and last reported client found error is on December 15th, 2025. \\n2. January 2026 quality at 100%.\\n3. Positive feedback shared by the client on last 2 monthly meetings.", "Result of Resolution": "Improved Relationship", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Manju Nath", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(03/09/2023):AHT analysis has been initiated and has been shared with clients during client connect on 03/02/2023. Follow up client connect scheduled in 2nd week of March 2023.\\n4-1(03/09/2023):AHT analysis discussion is ongoing and post client's confirmation, latest update will be shared by end of March 2023.\\n6-1(04/06/2023):Closing the RED CARE status as per the update received from Partnership Executive and Client Executive.\\n", "Parent Company": "HUB International Limited", "Account Name": "Specialty Program Group - Beacon Hill - Real Time - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "HUBSPGRTBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Anupama Rahul", "Supervisor": "Zaheed Wara", "Teamleader": "Anil Chandrashekar", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Client repeatedly complains or questions processing time", "Detailed Description": "Team is being over-utilized for about 3 months. Client raised a concern about AHT when we requested for additional staffing/over time.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2023, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Closing the RED CARE status as per the update received from Partnership Executive and Client Executive.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(02/21/2023):CE to follow up with client and notify SDU Team to update progress or close the issue in the C.A.R.E system.\\n5-1(03/10/2023):As of 3/10/2023, the Total Outstanding Balance: $8,481.94 for the following accounts:\\n\\nSpecialty Program Group - Regular - BGL\\nSpecialty Program Group - D&O Specialty team - Project\\n\\n6-1(04/12/2023):Payment received\\n", "Parent Company": "HUB International Limited", "Account Name": "Specialty Program Group - Beacon Hill - Regular - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "HUBSPGRGBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Mithra Amar", "Supervisor": "Abhishek Sampath", "Teamleader": "Chaitanya Pattem", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Client is 120+ days overdue to pay RSP", "Detailed Description": "Total Outstanding Balance: $22,102.54 for the following accounts:\\n\\nSpecialty Program Group - Regular - BGL\\nSpecialty Program Group - Real Time - BGL\\nSpecialty Program Group - D&O Specialty team - Project", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2023, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Payment received", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "HUB International Limited", "Account Name": "Specialty Program Group - Strategic Benefit Resources - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "HUBSPGSBRBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Mithra Amar", "Supervisor": "Arjun Chembai", "Teamleader": "Monica Alexander", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Pricing/Competitive Threat", "Issue Type": "Client sends notice of termination", "Detailed Description": "The account SBR (Strategic Benefit Resources) office was onboarded effective October 1, 2024; however, the client did not release any work until January 3, 2025, resulting in a three-month period with zero task allocation. During this time, the team was fully staffed and prepared, but with no productive workload assigned, the account experienced underutilization from the outset. Although the account is billed for 2 FTEs, the team has averaged only 1.2 FTEs of utilization over the last six months, highlighting a significant capacity gap.\\n\\nWe onboarded two tasks—Quote Entry and Claims—both involving updates to quote and claim information within the Salesforce application. Based on guidance from the SPG team, the assigned SBR members were temporarily deployed to assist the Compliance team in clearing backlog work, ensuring partial utilization during low-volume periods.\\n\\nIn the first week of November, Maryellen informed Helen (CE) and the team of the client’s decision to discontinue RSP support. The client cited improved efficiency within the Salesforce application and no longer requires manual assistance. This will impact RSP revenue. As per the client's request, we aligned the last working day as November 30, 2025.\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Resolution:\\n\\nUpon the additional follow-up by the CE, the client stated the decision was due to internal system efficiencies that eliminated the need for external processing support. Over the course of the engagement, team maintained consistent SLA performance and received positive feedback from the client.\\n \\nActions Taken / Completed:\\n\\n•The conclusion email was sent to the client on November 27 as requested.\\n\\n•All production activity on the account stopped effective December 1.\\n\\n•Resource allocation adjustments were completed following the account closure.\\n", "Result of Resolution": "Terminated", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "3-1(02/06/2025):As per the update received from PE, client has finalized the vendor and there will be no impact on the incoming volumes in 2025. \\n5-1(02/06/2025):As per the update received from PE, client has finalized the vendor and there will be no impact on the incoming volumes in 2025. \\n", "Parent Company": "HUB International Limited", "Account Name": "Specialty Program Group - Submission COE - Real Time - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "HUBSPGSRTBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Anupama Rahul", "Supervisor": "Shankar Johnny", "Teamleader": "Rahul Vora", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Pricing/Competitive Threat", "Issue Type": "Team finds client is working with another service provider", "Detailed Description": "Client requested BGL team to create a new account to track the Data capturing automation validation project.\\n\\nTeam found out that the data capturing automation for submissions from the source document will be used for an automation project (Submissions Clearance)", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": "As SDU is yet to determine the outcome of the automation project and the impact post implementation, we would like to raise YELLOW CARE status.", "Closed Reason": "As per the update received from PE, client has finalized the vendor and there will be no impact on the incoming volumes in 2025. ", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(02/13/2026):We started onboarding this client on March 10, 2025, and since then, the team has been experiencing lower volumes than anticipated. By May 2025, we had received only 19% of the forecasted volume. We have discussed this issue with the client during our regular calls. In June, we saw an improvement, receiving 39% of the forecasted volume. However, they might not meet the minimum annual billing requirement, If the volume trend continues to be low. It appears that not all account managers are using Policy Insights. Change management and not driving mandatory use of the PI are primary reasons for the low volume.\\n\\n6-1(02/24/2026):CE has proposed the client to move to Dedicated Team to improve the overall utilization. Client has signed the Contact for Dedicated Teram as of 2/23/2026. Closing the C.A.R.E as aligned with CE.\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Spectrum Insurance Group - PI - BGL", "Abbreviation": "SPECPIBGL", "Segment": "N", "Manager": "Kamal Kumar", "Supervisor": "Vyshak Valsarajan", "Teamleader": "Divya Gowda", "Client Executive": "Margery Schumick", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "7/31/2025: Following our monthly call with the client, we noticed an increase in volume for two weeks in June, but it decreased again in July. We have notified the client about the low volume. Brenda completed the Leader Analytics Dashboard training (Jul 18th) and the client remain engaged with CE. Below is the update from CE: Debra acknowledges that she needs to encourage higher utilization and has taken ownership of that. With last week's training, we hope Debra will make greater use of the leadership dashboard to start holding individuals accountable.\\n9/1/2025:We have not seen any improvement in incoming volume and aligned with CE to share the monthly billing summary with the client to keep them informed about both the revenue achieved and shortfall.\\n9/26/2025: Client started sending automatic renewal policies effective 9/18 to improve the utilization. \\n10/25/2025: In October, we received a volume of 138, which is below the monthly requirement of approximately 371 needed to meet the annual minimum billing. Since September 18, we've only received 51 automatic renewal policies.\\n12/3/2025: Margery contacted Debra (Client point of contact) and she inquired about our 'Auto Check' service with Margery. which she learned about at the Applied Conference. CE asked if we could offer the Auto Check service to the client. We shared our analysis with her, and she will follow up with the client and provide further details.\\n01/23/2026: CE discussed with the client the option of transferring their account from Policy Insights to a dedicated team. Due to current low volumes, this move will allow for greater flexibility to add additional tasks beyond policy checking to meet monthly minimums. The Policy Insights option can be revisited in a year or two, depending on their growth.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2026, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "CE has proposed the client to move to Dedicated Team to improve the overall utilization. Client has signed the Contact for Dedicated Teram as of 2/23/2026. Closing the C.A.R.E as aligned with CE.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Elvis Bailey", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(04/04/2024):Discussion with China team and BGL regular team to review the error happened on 03/27/2024\\nBasis the connect, response has been shared with China team - Addie Han and response has been acknowledged\\nBi-weekly connects with the BGL regular team is in place to review the transition status and to seek help and support\\n2-1(04/04/2024):SDU acknowledged the feedback and assured clients on sharing the detailed root cause analysis.\\n3-1(04/04/2024):Bi-weekly connects between China real-time, BGL real-time and with Clients are scheduled to review the transition status and the ongoing actions\\n4-1(04/04/2024):Root cause analysis has been completed and shared with clients on 03/29/2024\\n5-1(04/04/2024):Bi-weekly connect between SDU and clients are scheduled to review the transition status.\\n", "Parent Company": "HUB International Limited", "Account Name": "SPG Transportation - Real Time - Output - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "PHPRTOBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Shafath Khan", "Supervisor": "Shafath Khan", "Teamleader": "Shafath Khan", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Client complains about other production issue", "Detailed Description": "Client questions a rush \"LMD PKG Bind Order Review - New\" task being rejected by Bangalore Real Time\\n\\n1) Request came in at 7:20 AM on Thursday 3/21 and BLR RT picked up the case\\n2) Without checking with CN RT, or reviewing the request properly, BLR RT emailed client at 10:24 AM advising \"RT team is not trained to handle re-open Bind Order request\"\\n3) Client emailed CN RT for input at 10:29 AM\\n4) CN RT advised all parties at 10:35 AM the request was a routine task for RT and proper training was completed\\n5) BLR RT completed the task and provided an update to all at 4:36 PM\\n6) This is a repeating issue as the very same issue happened in February where client questioned why the same type of routine task was rejected by BLR RT\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "BGL real-time received the required training steps from the BGL regular shift and performed 1 case as well.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "HUB International Limited", "Account Name": "SPG Transportation - Real Time - Output - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "PHPRTOBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Shafath Khan", "Supervisor": "Shafath Khan", "Teamleader": "Shafath Khan", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Client complains about other quality issues", "Detailed Description": "Client has raised an concern on repeated miss outs on communication. Request was assigned to BGL real-time at 7:06 AM (PST) and has 2 hour turn around completion and team missed to complete the case with in turn around time and took 3.5 hours. Client reached out on Teams and 10:30 AM (PST) and did not receive an update for 30 minutes on the status of the case and sent an email to the BGL real time PHP team.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Client is satisfied with the ongoing action plan reviewed during the bi-weekly connect and acknowledged the communication has improved.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Account Name": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Abbreviation": "SIGL", "Segment": "N", "Manager": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Supervisor": "Sandeep Udaya", "Teamleader": "Anil Ramaiah", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Pricing/Competitive Threat", "Issue Type": "Client sends notice of termination", "Detailed Description": "Background :11/21- Jill Quinn of Sunstar Ins.(Insurancenter parent company) has questioned why Insurancenter is being charged a $1,000 monthly management fee when Insurancenter has 2 FTE’s and Sunstar has 2 FTE’s,  they were under the impression they would not be charged a management fee. SDU provided the option of combining both the teams to save the management cost.\\n\\nClient Response - Jill has indicated they do not want to combine their team with Insurancenter at this time… as they are taking a hard look at the teams production/support and their overall spend.  She indicated RSP may not be the best solution for Sunstar going forward. Jill is getting pressure to look at alternate support therefore she says it does not make sense to combine teams to reduce the management fee, only to have to reinstate the fee if Sunstar decides to move off of RSP\\nHowever, Jill indicated the team’s accuracy is good, she feels the volume of work being completed in comparison to what her Account Managers are completing is low.  Jill’s AM’s have expressed concern that they are working overtime to support the volume of work coming in… and they’re seeing the team working 7 hrs. a day with their final production being much lower to that of the US.\\n\\n01/13/2023 - Jill spoke to the CE and informed that they have made a decision to bring the teams work back in house. They have hired two US team members that are currently in training to take over the team’s work.\\nShe noted this was not due to the team’s efforts, it’s really due to their highly customized needs, the amount of back and forth on clarification etc.  She noted they are not going with another vender as that would not\\nmake sense they have hired internal US staff. She noted the pricing and cost would be the same.\\nJill indicated they plan to continue with the team’s support through Mid February and will be providing a formal written notice of termination next week.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Client has sent notice of termination. 02/15 is the last day of service.", "Result of Resolution": "Terminated", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "The Baldwin Insurance Group Holdings, LLC", "Account Name": "The Baldwin Insurance Group Holdings, LLC - Accounting - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "BKSBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Sourav Basu", "Supervisor": "Pearline Clara", "Teamleader": "Sushma Bhakthiraju", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Pricing/Competitive Threat", "Issue Type": "Client requests to reduce team size", "Detailed Description": "Bangalore Team Terminated.\\n\\nBackground:\\n03/22 -India SDU team onboarded Mail indexing task from China SDU team as the client preferred BCP coverage. The client had confirmed that once the transition is over, India SDU team will onboard more offices.\\n12/21 -China SDU team has onboarded this task from the client. However, the range price was not approved by the client as they had concerns on the unit price proposed at $1.99 and 4.5 mins AHT and their expectations was below $1.99.\\n05/09 - Bangalore team completed the transition and continued to bill on hourly rate as the CCF was not signed.\\nSDU Action - Continuous follow up with the CE to check on the onboarding of other offices.\\nInitiated monthly governance call with the clients. CE change from Tracy - Adam - Brett\\n11/18 - SDU proposed a revised CCF to the CE, with $1.92 unit price and 4.35 mins AHT.\\n11/18 - 02/14 - Followed up with the CE on the CCF proposal. The CE was unable to meet the client.\\n02/14 - The CE shared the proposed the CCF to the client - Due to the annual price increase; the unit price was changed to $1.99\\n02/22 - The client informed on taking the process in house so that they can leverage their underutilized staff\\n03/09 - The CE  informed on the notice of termination sent by the client. However, waiting to hear from the CE on the actual notice of termination date.\\nApril -  CE is checking with the client to determine the last charge date and is also working on a long term plan for the BGL team\\n 05/15 - The CE sent an email that the client has has advised a transition date of July 5th and the team at BKS to fully take over the Mail indexing. Last service date would by 5th Jul 2023. \\nFrom 6th Jul, the client will take over the entire volume.\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2023, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Last day of service as per client request- 07/07", "Result of Resolution": "Terminated", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Elvis Bailey", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "The Baldwin Insurance Group Holdings, LLC", "Account Name": "The Baldwin Insurance Group Holdings, LLC - Accounting - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "BKSBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Sourav Basu", "Supervisor": "Pearline Clara", "Teamleader": "Sushma Bhakthiraju", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Client reports multiple errors by the team or a processor", "Detailed Description": "Client identified two errors for one task PRM - Update Renewal Program Summary task", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Team has been provided with:\\n. Increased 100% audits for the team for 2 weeks and no findings from client side.\\n. Conducted regular procedure review \\nand teach back sessions regularly.", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Elvis Bailey", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(02/14/2022):Detailed analysis of AHT and production trend shared with CE. Requested time to schedule a call and walk through the data\\n", "Parent Company": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Account Name": "The Insurancenter", "Abbreviation": "TSC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Sajjad Ahmed", "Client Executive": "Margery Schumick", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "In a meeting with CE, clients have expressed concerns on team's average handling times. They have indicated that team is consistently not meeting their expectations on the average handling times and the turn around times. When the CE suggested we complete a task review to make sure the team was not completing extra steps, they indicated they had sent recording over to the team, and the team had sent recordings back over to them. Noting in the video the processor was completing the work timely, but they were not seeing that daily.\\n\\nThey also indicated they had had two of SunStar organizations reach out to them to work with ReSource Pro.  They indicated the offices should hold off for now.\\n\\n\\n ", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2022, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "SDU team shared a AHT target plan on the below-mentioned tasks with the CE on April 22nd. \\n\\nPolicy Checking – Monoline :80\\nPolicy Checking – Package:130\\nEndorsement Checking: 45\\nPremium Audit:30\\nPolicy Checking – Bonds:45\\nExp-Mod Report:60\\n\\nMay 6th: Received a note from the CE that the CARE alert can be removed and we can monitor the AHT as per the agreed AHT. \\n- Raise an alert if we hear / receive feedback again from the client team. \\n- SDU acknowledged to the CE  on May 9th 2022. \\n", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(10/12/2022):SDU team had discussion with CE on 10/11/2022\\n\\nCE to discuss with clients on the proposed process improvement suggestions and provide further direction to SDU\\n4-1(01/10/2023):Team has shared the performance report for November and December, and has not received any feedback from client on AHT\\n\\nIn the month of December, key client contact Diane complimented the team for being current on all work and gave a day off to the team\\n\\n*CE requested for a meeting with clients to discuss team performance. Diane Hendrickson who is the key client contact is leaving  Insurancenter effective 11th January 2023.  Dwan Oney will take over as key contact and she would like to meet in February as she currently has a busy schedule\\n", "Parent Company": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Account Name": "The Insurancenter", "Abbreviation": "TSC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Sajjad Ahmed", "Client Executive": "Margery Schumick", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Client repeatedly complains or questions processing time", "Detailed Description": "CE had a meeting with client on 09/30/2022, and clients have expressed concern that teams AHT is still running high. Below is the summary:\\n\\n‘I joined a call today with Diane from Insurancenter she indicated the teams support times are still running much higher than expected.  With that said they have already pulled some of the processing work back to have this work supported by a US based BPM Service, Wave.  Wave employs US based Lisc. Support.   Diane mentioned their Mod work that they took back was taking our team 2 to 3 hours, 1 Mod took our team 8 hours, where the Wave EE, who had never processed this type of work before, was able to complete the work in 30 to 60 minutes working in Zywave.  She indicated Bond work which was taking ReSource Pro’s team 50 minutes was taking their 1 Wave EE 15 or 20 minutes.’ \\n\\nSDU Analysis:\\n\\nMod work: This is a low volume task, and team received 25 cases YTD (August) and all have been completed with TAT. In May 2022, team received 6 cases of which 4 were complex. They had 10 to 18 losses against normal average of 2 losses. ResourcePro standard AHT for this task is 40-60 minutes. The examples Diane shared with Low AHT have 0-1 losses \\n\\nBond work – This is also a low volume task, and team received 24 cases YTD (August) and all have been completed within TAT. ResourcePro standard AHT for this task is 20 – 60 minutes.\\n\\nClients had expressed concern on AHT in March, 2022 as well. Opex team conducted a detailed process analysis and provided process improvement suggestions to reduce AHT in policy checking. CE had shared these recommendations with the clients in July 2022, but we have still not received go ahead from the clients to implement the suggestions.\\n\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "CE met with Key client contact Dawn, summary of discussion:\\n\\n \"I met with Dawn this morning, she is extremely happy with the team’s work, therefore it does not sound like she will be moving the team away from RSP, so please close the CARE alert.  Dawn did note they do have 1 to 2 WAVE EE’s supporting their work as well.  \\nAs they are having difficulty finding AM support in the US, I walked her through our Premier FTE staffing model noting I will provide her additional detail after our call.  Dawn plans on reviewing the information and getting back to me directly.\"\\n", "Result of Resolution": "Improved Relationship", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(10/28/2022):CE to follow up with client and notify SDU Team to update progress or close the issue in the C.A.R.E system.\\n6-1(01/20/2023):Payment received\\n", "Parent Company": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Account Name": "The Insurancenter", "Abbreviation": "TSC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Sajjad Ahmed", "Client Executive": "Margery Schumick", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Client is 120+ days overdue to pay RSP", "Detailed Description": "Total Outstanding Balance: $7,840.06", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Payment received", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "6-1(09/19/2018):We have updated the internal audit errors on the supervisor portal not tracked the feedbacks received from Client (On boarded Policy checking in June and Endorsement checking in August, these feedbacks included errors and updates so we have not updated any feedback from June), hence there is difference in numbers.\\nControl Measures: \\n1. We will start tracking Diane’s feedback as client found error in the supervisor portal and for the New Scenarios, updates we will get it approved by the Diane.\\n2. We will start sharing post audit results in the Daily Production Log\\n3. We will start sharing Volumes and Quality details in the Weekly report.\\n4. In addition, we will add all the feedbacks on the portal, which allows us to be in line with client data.\\n\\na. Okay\\nb. Okay\\n6-2(10/02/2018):Team member will send email to team lead after logging off from the TAM application on daily basis. Team members have started sending email post logging off from TAM application from 09/20 and it will be ongoing process and we have not encountered any TAM issues. \\n6-3(09/19/2018):We will surely try our best to inform as soon as possible, to give background details team here login into system by 8:00 AM and if they encounter any system issue first they need to escalate it to internal IT support team and then based on their inputs we have to reroute to Diane and hence notifying issue by 8:00 AM is challenging.\\n6-4(09/19/2018):We agree with the client and since we are monitoring the team performance on daily & weekly basis, there will be ongoing improvement and we will surely bring down question/error to below 10%.\\n", "Parent Company": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Account Name": "The Insurancenter", "Abbreviation": "TSC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Sajjad Ahmed", "Client Executive": "Margery Schumick", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "1. Client provided feedback that question/error rate of 33% which is different than the 2% error rate reflected on the MIR report. Client need to understand the discrepancy between the numbers. \\na. Please add Cheryl Kusick back to all daily correspondence so she can review volume of questions and audit feedback from Client. \\nb. Please create a Weekly Report of the question/errors we can provide to Client so we can reconcile the question/error% on a weekly basis.\\n\\n2. Please make sure team is logging off of TAM at the end of each day. Client has noticed that the ReSourcePro is not logging off consistently out of TAM. Not logging out will lock the user out of TAM when they run the nightly utility program which will then require an access reset. Client mentioned this happens frequently.\\n\\n3. Please notify Client of any system access issues at the beginning of the shift so she is not contacted late at night. 8:00am Bangalore time should be 10:30pm EST.\\n\\n4. Client doesn’t want to move forward with on boarding Change Request and Endorsements until client is not checking 100% of Renewal Policies and Endorsements. Therefore, we need to drive down the 33% question/error rate to below 10% by mid-October to target starting the onboarding of the additional processes as of November 1st. ", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2018, "Closed Year": 2018, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Based on Client feedback, there has been improvement in Quality and we closing the issue.", "Result of Resolution": "Improved Relationship", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "Sunstar Insurance Group, LLC", "Account Name": "The Insurancenter", "Abbreviation": "TSC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Sajjad Ahmed", "Client Executive": "Margery Schumick", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Client repeatedly complains or questions processing time", "Detailed Description": "I have provided a summary with timeline \\n\\n8/12 – Diane shared an email with revised targets Package policy checking: 140 minutes, Monoline policy checking: 75 minutes, Endorsement checking: 40 minutes, Audit checking: 25 minutes\\n\\n8/12 – Diane requested for a daily report only on pure production / processing time. \\n\\n8/13- Shared the action plan with Fatima. \\n\\n8/16 - The SDU team provided a plan on the request from Diane on the new targets and the daily report. \\nThe SDU team have been meeting the targets from Feb 2021 – till date as per the agreed targets with the client (Diane). \\n\\n8/19 – Dawn VP from the client team talked to Cheryl (As the account was onboarded in 2018 by Cheryl),  raising concerns on quality, processing time taken on mod master task and processing questions, not having a CE for 2 months and thinking of pulling their account from ReSource Pro. Cheryl mentioned that the team would provide an action plan. \\n\\n8/20 – SDU team provided a detailed analysis in continuation to the 8/13 email correspondence. \\n\\nNext Steps: Fatima will schedule a call with Dawn in the coming week. \\n\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2021, "Closed Year": 2021, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Had a meeting with the client team on 9/8. \\nThe client provided positive feedback about the analysis and the progress we have made on Questions. ", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(02/24/2025):1. The audit ratio was raised to 100%.\\n2. The team was informed about the knowledge deficiency and the strategy to address the errors.\\n3. The procedure was revised based on the new insights.\\n4. Arranged meetings with the Client Certs SME to address process discrepancies and review additional scenarios.\\n4-1(03/06/2025):1. Experienced team members have been designated to oversee.\\n2. The team consistently performs 100% audits on all requests before sending it to the client.\\n3. In cases of uncertainty, the team has been instructed to contact the client for clarification rather than making assumptions.\\n4. Document any updates or clarifications provided by the client in the procedure and share them with team members.\\n5. Any queries directed to the client will be reviewed by the team leader.\\n5-1(03/18/2025):Client provided positive feedback and called out that everything is progressing well.\\n5-2(03/21/2025):Client provided positive feedback and called out that everything is progressing well\\n6-1(03/21/2025):Closing CARE as per CEs confirmation\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The McClone Agency, Inc. - Certs Center", "Abbreviation": "TMACERT", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Anthony Kanthan", "Supervisor": "Naveen Kumar", "Teamleader": "Chandra Reddy", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Client reports multiple errors by the team or a processor", "Detailed Description": "The account was onboarded on 12/06/24, and the first feedback was received on 01/31/25. The client has identified 11 errors. which were attributed to clerical and understanding issues. An action plan to address these errors was shared on 02/05/24. On 02/20, the client expressed concerns about the on-boarder and team leader's understanding of the Certificate process, and requested a complete overhaul of the team. On 02/21, details of the new team member with experience in certificates were shared with the client. Starting from 02/24/25, the new team members will be managing this account.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Client confirmed that everything is progressing well and feels confident about the new team", "Result of Resolution": "Improved Relationship", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Aniruddha Gupta", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The Redwoods Group, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "RWGO", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kavyak Babu", "Supervisor": "Sharada Chandra", "Teamleader": "Manju Biradar", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Client reports multiple errors by the team or a processor", "Detailed Description": "09/01 – Received feedback for a specific policy - for Greater Burlington YMCA , was done one day prior to renewal and was sent directly to the broker.  This should have been sent out on 7/15 \\nsince the state of VT requires 45 days and should not have been sent to the broker.\\n\\nRCA - Clear miss from the processor to work on this renewal as he overlooked the response email from the underwriter.\\n\\n09/02 - The SDU team has shared the action plan with the CE and this has been shared with the client", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2022, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Performance for September has been better with 1 client found error. Client is happy with the progress.\\nCE is aligned to move the alert back to Green.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The Redwoods Group, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "RWGO", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kavyak Babu", "Supervisor": "Sharada Chandra", "Teamleader": "Manju Biradar", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Point person at the client side changes", "Detailed Description": "Background :\\n­Mar24-  Leadership change – From Amy to Robin – Main point of Contact /Decision Maker\\nJul24 – Robin called out they would like to take back 2 tasks - Account Payable and Processing Cash which is equivalent to 0.3 FTE work. This was effective 09/02. The was due to available in house capacity at the client side.\\n­Aug24 – Reached out to SDU on partial supporting for US time zone. SDU has reached out for more information. \\n­Sep24 – Robin wants to transition back Conditional Notices effective 12/01 which is again equivalent to 0.3 FTE\\n\\n09/05 -Action taken by SDU:\\nReached out to the CE calling out the recent events and requesting more information on client's future strategies.\\n09/05 - CE reverted stating the following-\\nShe  had a discussion with Robin and Alisha on Friday, and they told her that as of July 1 Redwoods officially transitioned back to Crum & Forester, meaning Redwoods will no longer be operating autonomously.  That’s the reason they are taking back some tasks. In addition, they are going through another set of layoffs as of the end of Sept.  This will include Robin and Alisha.  Paige (President &COO of Redwoods) has sent her an email today so she will work directly with her to find out who will be our point person going forward.  The loss of Alisha as our point person will have an effect.\\nThey didn’t want to tell the SDU team until they figured things out on their side. The CE will update the team once she speaks to Paige.\\n\\nUpdate from the CE - 09/18:\\n1.As of July 1 Redwoods is now under the Crum & Forster umbrella and staff from Crum will be our new contacts as of Oct 1. \\n2.Sheri Singh, AVP Operations, Crum, Stephanie Albanese, Crum & Brandi Dickey will be our main contacts.\\n3.They have already made significant UW changes and 1 broker is moving an entire book of business to another carrier.\\n4.Condition notice task will see reduced volumes and ZERO by Nov.\\n5.Fatima and Ernie are meeting with Ken Russo from Crum at WSIA next wee", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "10/29 -Fatima had a discussion with Paige(Redwoods Clients) who mentioned they don't have a drop date of no longer working with ReSource Pro. It may just be they just eliminate some tasks and keep others. No decisions have been made at this point.  ", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "6-1(01/22/2018):1. To escalate the issue and get the IT access at the earliest, which also allows us to start processing.\\n2. To highlight the client on the low volumes, so that we receive acceptable number of volume from the clients.\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The Redwoods Group, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "RWGO", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kavyak Babu", "Supervisor": "Sharada Chandra", "Teamleader": "Manju Biradar", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "IT/Systems", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "1. Did not receive the access to select producer on Submission system. As a result we have not been able to do the task for the 10 working days against our task onboarding plan.\\n\\n2. Overall volume is very low, due to which we do not have enough exposure on different scenarios.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2018, "Closed Year": 2018, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Received system access and seen increase in volume for the team", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The Redwoods Group, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "RWGO", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kavyak Babu", "Supervisor": "Sharada Chandra", "Teamleader": "Manju Biradar", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "July 2024 - Redwoods officially transitioned back to Crum & Forester, meaning Redwoods will no longer be operating autonomously.\\nPosts that they have taken back 2 tasks in Sep24,1 in Nov24 and 2 tasks in April25 - CARE alert was recorded for this.\\nHowever, the team continued to witness a gradual decrease in revenue. Based on this SDU initiated a call with the CE and the client. The client mentioned the reason for the decrease in volume and revenue is due to the following reasons.\\n1) Loss of primary producer \\n2) Have gone from 72 employees to ~20\\n3)45% loss in premiums\\nThe client confirmed SDU can continue to use the current forecast pattern and will revaluate the situation in Jul25\\nDiscussion with the clients to explore other opportunities that would support their core commercial lines.\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Paige suggested maintaining the current forecasting approach. By doing so, the team met the forecasted volumes and revenue for May and June. CE agreed on this and closed the CARE alert.", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact,Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The Redwoods Group, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "RWGO", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kavyak Babu", "Supervisor": "Sharada Chandra", "Teamleader": "Manju Biradar", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Point person at the client side changes", "Detailed Description": "03/11 - Received an email from the client point of contact stating some recent, unexpected changes within Redwoods. \\nRedwoods had to make the difficult decision to lay off 20 employees across various departments late last week. These changes are a part of their strategic efforts to streamline operations and enhance profitability. Consequently, they have had to reduce their staff size and implement immediate changes in underwriting and pricing.\\nThe client mentioned her tenure at Redwoods will conclude on March 29th, marking the end of her 18th year with the company.\\n03/12 - SDU and the CE had a call with the client to understand this more in detailed and the impact for ReSource Pro. Based on the call, as of now, there is no significant change for ReSource Pro. However, the SDU team has seen an increase in volume for the AU work.\\nAs next steps, the client will confirm on the volume impact based on the recent changes.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Blue", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "New client Point of Contact - Robin has been introduced. At this point there is no impact to the client relationship and volume inflow.", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "The Redwoods Group, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "RWGO", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kavyak Babu", "Supervisor": "Sharada Chandra", "Teamleader": "Manju Biradar", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Client directs taking back a task(s)", "Detailed Description": "Received an email from Robin (Client) stating they want to take back 2 tasks as they want to utilize some new internal resources. This will be effective 09/01\\n• Account Payable\\n• Processing Cash\\nThey did state that they are happy SDU team's services but it makes sense for them to manage these in-house going forward. \\nThe monthly revenue for both the tasks is ~$700\\nConsidering there was a leadership change 6 months back; triggered this on CARE", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Blue", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Raised this for awareness. ", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Akhilaa Hariharan", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(08/03/2023):Periodic connect with Clients to discuss on team's performance. \\n4-1(08/03/2023):SDU is receiving volumes since February 2023 and FTE utilization is 2.38 - April'23 ; 2.14 - May'23; 1.65 - June'23 and 2.14 - July'23\\n5-1(08/03/2023):FE utilization and available capacity will be shared with clients on periodic governance calls and SDU will request clients to allocate new task to utilize the available capacity.\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Tokio Marine Highland - Real Time", "Abbreviation": "WNC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Mohan Balekundri", "Supervisor": "Somanna Boppanda", "Teamleader": "Vijaya Lakshmi", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Team is underutilized by half a FTE or more for longer than one month with unknown reason", "Detailed Description": "1. Currently, the team has onboarded 12 different tasks from the client and not receiving enough volume to achieve 2 FTE’s work.\\n2. All the existing tasks volume inflow is low compared to a month on month. Also, we brought this concern up in our monthly check-in meeting with the client and proposed new tasks to onboard. However, the team is unable to achieve 2 FTE’s work after onboarding 12 different tasks.\\n3. For the last four months, the team is underutilized, for May - 78%, June - 74%, July - 59%, and August - 62%. Which is keep reducing month on month.\\n4. The client has approved, the 3rd charged FTE for new tasks like Surplus Line taxes, Report generation, and Billing duties tasks. However, not getting enough volumes on the existing task to achieve 2 FTE the client has approved 3rd FTE.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "SDU is receiving volumes since February 2023 and FTE utilization is 2.38 FTE - April'23 ; 2.14 FTE - May'23; 1.65 FTE - June'23 and 2.14 FTE - July'23", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(09/30/2022):CE to follow up with client and notify SDU Team to update progress or close the issue in the C.A.R.E system.\\n1-2(02/01/2023):CE confirmed that the client is working on getting it paid.  It should happen soon.\\n5-1(02/01/2023):CE confirmed that the client is working on getting it paid.  It should happen soon.\\n6-1(03/10/2023):Payment received\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Tokio Marine Highland - Real Time", "Abbreviation": "WNC", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Mohan Balekundri", "Supervisor": "Somanna Boppanda", "Teamleader": "Vijaya Lakshmi", "Client Executive": "Dan Tharp", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Client is 120+ days overdue to pay RSP", "Detailed Description": "Total Outstanding Balance: $6,639.54", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2023, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Payment received", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(05/29/2024):5/21-5/23: Upon receiving the impact client and policy list, the PI SDU team cross-verified the information between the AMP review summaries and the client's AMS to identify if any downstream steps have been taken. The investigation results were shared with the Product team and Technology team on 5/23.\\n5/28: The Product team led the communication with the BD team to define the client communication approach for this issue.\\n3-1(05/30/2024):Philip communicated with the client about this issue, and we are waiting for the client's feedback.\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Towne Insurance - PI - BGL", "Abbreviation": "TOWNEPIBGL", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Kamal Kumar", "Supervisor": "Sharan Mahagonkar", "Teamleader": "Sachin Sheshagiri", "Client Executive": "Jeff Jones", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "IT/Systems", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "It has been identified on 5/17 that two Account Manager Portal (AMP) emails were missed to be delivered to the account managers on 2/21. The Technology team, Product team, and SDU team have been working on checking more details about these missing emails in order to evaluate the impact on our client and determine the next steps. This client also experienced duplicate and missing email issues that were reported on 3/2.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2024, "Closed Year": 2024, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "We have not received a response from the client even after multiple follow-ups. Hence closing the CARE alert.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Elvis Bailey", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(04/07/2022):OA has discussed the issue with the clients during team meetings. Clients had informed that they are working to ramp up the volumes. Volumes increased slightly during the second half of February but it was not sufficient to meet the monthly minimum billing requirements.\\n\\n", "Parent Company": "Patriot Growth Insurance Services LLC", "Account Name": "Western Agency, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "WEAG", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Shwetha Nandesh", "Client Executive": "Skip Disbrow", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Production", "Issue Type": "Output client with work volume at monthly minimum consistently for over a month", "Detailed Description": "Western Agency account was onboarded in November 2021 and team has not met the monthly minimum billing till March. All the in scope tasks have been on boarded. Additional 2 new tasks have also been onboarded in February", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2022, "Closed Year": 2022, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Revenue for the month of April improved to $6,433, short by only $67 for minimum billing\\n\\nClient has given an additional task and team has started onboarding this task from 05/01/2022. This will further improve the revenue", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "Patriot Growth Insurance Services LLC", "Account Name": "Western Agency, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "WEAG", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Shwetha Nandesh", "Client Executive": "Skip Disbrow", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "IT/Systems", "Issue Type": "Client system is down causing team unable to access the system for longer than a day", "Detailed Description": "Since February 10th, 2025, our team has encountered challenges in accessing Cloud PC RDP client server. The issue has been escalated to the client's team looping CE, who are currently working on resolving it.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Blue", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "Effective February 13, 2025, the systems are operational and functioning smoothly. We successfully accessed the client server without encountering any issues. Over the last two days, we have been monitoring the system to ensure its consistent performance, and we have not faced any problems thus far.", "Result of Resolution": "No Impact", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": "Patriot Growth Insurance Services LLC", "Account Name": "Western Agency, Inc. - Output", "Abbreviation": "WEAG", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Deepti Nanjunda", "Supervisor": "Dinesh Erakattu", "Teamleader": "Shwetha Nandesh", "Client Executive": "Skip Disbrow", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Client directs taking back a task(s)", "Detailed Description": "Background\\nThe Western Agency (WEAG) account is an output-based account started in Nov 2021, and is part of the parent company, Patriot.\\nCurrently, we support the account across 15 tasks with an FTE output of 4 to 5 FTEs\\n\\nTimeline of Events\\n• 11/17 – Received a request from Bob Monrad, CFO, for the accounting procedures following the departure of an employee from Western Agency.\\n• 12/16 – Received a note from Jackie Larson, the primary contact for the agency, confirming the decision to move four accounting tasks in-house, effective December 16, 2025, resulting in an FTE impact of 0.26.\\n\\nVolume & FTE Impact \\nTotal Tasks: 4 | Average Monthly Volume: 3,638 | Average Monthly Revenue (2025): $1,226.41 |Quality YTD : 99.99%  | FTE Impact: 0.26 \\n\\nNext Steps: \\n\\nRequesting the CE to confirm whether the client is\\n\\n1. Exploring any automation opportunities, or\\n2. Has hired an internal employee to support these accounting tasks.\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Blue", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "12/16 – Received a note from Jackie Larson, the primary contact for the agency to Allison with SDU in loop - There is  really no additional information to share, the accounting department is simply able to handle their work load and decided to keep it in house.\\n\\nThanks so much for your work on these things in the past, we appreciate your willingness to help fill our needs.\\n\\nClosing this alert as per the email confirmation.\\n", "Result of Resolution": "Reduced FTE(s)", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(03/08/2025):Fatima Dean and Fernanda Rosen will be meeting with the client's decision-makers to discuss possible solutions. They will also present the various services that RSP can offer and propose an Output model for billing as an alternative solution.\\n6-1(04/10/2025):1. Fatima will connect with Carlie to discuss the proposal to add an FTE or implement an output model during the Summit in April 2025.\\n2. Fatima and Fernanda Rosen will meet with Eric Richter (CEO/President) and Jake Goin (COO/CFO) onsite in May/June 2025 to discuss the services RSP can provide and plan their budget.\\n\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Western Pacific Insurance Network, Inc. and Virtus Underwriting Group, Inc. - Output - RT - BGL", "Abbreviation": "WVIRTBGL", "Segment": "B", "Manager": "Satish Marudhukavil", "Supervisor": "Libitha Senthil", "Teamleader": "Vinod Kumar", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Pricing/Competitive Threat", "Issue Type": "Client reports that they are working with another provider", "Detailed Description": "In a recent communication on 3/4, the client has informed us that they plan to reassign all Submission setup tasks to another outsourcing team. The aim is to complete this transition by 04/01/2025. The primary reason for this decision is that the BGL-RT team is fully occupied, and the client prefers not to add additional FTE in RSP. Instead, they intend to utilize the available capacity in RT to onboard PL Quote tasks starting from 4/1 to make the most of the team's resources and available capacity. Client has also mentioned that this decision has nothing to do with the team’s quality of work and appreciated the team for the service delivery.", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Fatima and Fernanda Rosen will meet the clients during Summit in Apr’25 and onsite in May/June 2025 to discuss output model and the services RSP can provide and plan their budget.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Nimit Advani", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "6-1(01/16/2026):Account will be monitored for any significant impact on utilization or non receipt of new tasks in pipeline.\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "WHA Insurance Agency Inc. - Real Time", "Abbreviation": "WHA", "Segment": "N", "Manager": "Anupama Rahul", "Supervisor": "Gouri Shankar", "Teamleader": "Charan Theja", "Client Executive": "Skip Disbrow", "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Point person at the client side changes", "Detailed Description": "On May 19, the BGL SDU team started onboarding the account WHA Insurance Agencies, Inc. for 2 FTEs, with the primary contact being Cody King (Chief Revenue Officer).\\nOn June 11, Michelle Javinar (OA) was notified of a new point of contact at WHA, Traci Rose (Chief Operating Officer), who will be primarily involved in decision-making alongside Cody.\\nTask priority (client):\\n\\n• Backlogs – QC Policy (550) and QC Endorsements (1000)\\n• Post Renewals\\n• Remaining tasks as decided by WHA\\nTask Transition status:\\n• Original Transition Plan Task count – 13\\n• Knowledge transfer completed – 6\\n• Onboarded – 2 (May – June)\\n• Currently onboarding -1 (November - December)\\nBacklog status:\\n• Completed on October 31, 2025.\\nPerformance summary from May to Nov 2025\\n3425 transactions | 1 error | Quality Score: 99.97%| Utilization: 1.85 FTE \\nClient Communication\\nOn September 4, the SDU team was informed that 7 tasks included in the original plan would be retained in-house, including 4 tasks for which knowledge transfer had already been completed. Subsequently, the client informed the team that remaining tasks in proposal would not be transitioned to Resource Pro. Instead, they would evaluate tasks within other WHA departments that could be transferred to Resource Pro to ensure utilization of the 2 FTEs.\\n\\nSDU Actions:\\n• Any underutilization has been reported to the client on a weekly basis and documented in MIRs.\\n• The team completed knowledge transfer for the task “Post Renewals” on December 10, 2025, and is awaiting volumes for testing.\\nClient Connects:\\n• The SDU team has been meeting with the client on a weekly basis and presenting progress on completed work, for which the client has expressed appreciation.\\n• The SDU team, along with Allison and Michelle, has been regularly following up with Traci regarding new tasks that can be transitioned. As of the last conversation on December 10, the client is still in the decision-making process.\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2026, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Account will be monitored for any significant impact on utilization or non receipt of new tasks in pipeline. A new CARE alert will be raised based on the results.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Ashish Kumar", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "1-1(05/20/2021):Action Plan:\\n\\nTurnaround Time –  We have rearranged the shift timings of our team members on a rotational basis to have a few team members log in advance of the rest of the team to clear backlogs from the previous day if needed, we have developed an updated queue management plan with additional monitoring of the mailboxes and an updated prioritization of work. We are already seeing benefits with these changes as we were able to hit all targets last week and improved turnaround time by 30 minutes for non-rush requests and 20 minutes for rush requests compared to April.\\n\\nQuality: We have taken the following steps though the plan is a work in progress: we held a workshop led by Cathy Trischan our external consultant on reviewing requests, contract review and what to look for on construction certificates, we increased our audit percentage for importing holder edits and spent time with the team reiterating the importance of sending out the emails from the common mailbox ID and not their individual emails. We are conducting a further analysis on errors and will be sharing it with the client on our call on 5/21. \\n\\nCapacity – We have created a daily capacity ramp- up plan for the months of May, June & July using forecasted volumes from the client and will be sharing it with the client weekly ensuring we hit our targets. Our renewal capacity remains and we are on track to be able to handle all renewal certificates for 6/1 provided the client gives us enough lead time.                                                       \\n\\n\\n", "Parent Company": "Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. (Hold)", "Account Name": "Woodruff Sawyer & Company - Certs Center - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "WSCCERTBGL", "Segment": "A", "Manager": "Vidya Shree", "Supervisor": "Asha Shankar", "Teamleader": "Prashanth Murthy", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Client Relationship", "Issue Type": "Other", "Detailed Description": "Issues: Client has brought up issues related to bandwidth, turnaround time, and quality over the recent weeks in addition the team has been impacted by team members with COVID-19 and had instances where we were unable to complete daily work due to power outages. The client remains committed to the relationship but has notified us that they are considering alternative options for some of their more complex requests. \\n\\nThe team including Tony (CE), Brenda, and SDU are working diligently and collaboratively on addressing the issues and have kept the China team informed. While we are confident we can resolve these issues we wanted to raise them:\\n\\nTurnaround Time - Melissa Schellinkhout, Pacific Northwest Practice Leader, highlighted on the 04/23 weekly call that there have been instances when ReSource Pro has taken more than 24 hours to issue certificates.\\n\\nQuality– Renewals - Melissa highlighted on the 05/07 weekly call that there were 2 cases of high profile renewal accounts where errors of holder edits had occurred. On –demand - Laura Kearney, Practice Leader Southern California, highlighted via email on 05/11 that the team should send the certificates out from the common mailbox ID, and not their individual email IDs. Also we had 4 client found errors on Construction accounts in April which caused the client to question our ability to handle these types of accounts.       \\n\\nCapacity/ Ramp Up – In 2021 we have been aggressively ramping up production for both ondemand & renewal certificates and set a target of being able to handle full volume for the 4 offices we are working with by 6/1 which was behind their initial expectations but was agreed to. The team looked set to hit both the on demand and renewal target however beginning in early May (1st instance on 05/04) the team began being impacted by COVID 19 with multiple team members out of the office with the virus each day which has impacted our ramp up time for on-demand certificates.\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2021, "Closed Year": 2021, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Yellow", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "-Client has indicated they are satisfied with progress and are planning on adding new offices. The team was able to handle full volume for 6/1 renewals and has excess capacity to take on, on demand certificates beginning in July.\\n-Quality levels have improved.\\n-The client has requested to reduce the frequency of regular calls as they are pleased with progress. \\n\\nMore scope- Renewals 100%, more capacity, possibly handle new locations\\n", "Result of Resolution": "Improved Relationship", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "RealTime", "Director": "Aniruddha Gupta", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "7-1(10/30/2025):Clients raised Pricing/Competitive concern:\\n\\nBackground:\\n\\nOn Oct 28th, the client has requested a reduction in 2026 rates or several months free for the errors made. On July 17th, during a call with Margery Schumick, the client raised concerns about the quality errors, and Christian Wright (Client team) requested the account to be moved back to China. \\n\\nAfter our root cause analysis and action plan were implemented, the quality status after July 2025 is mentioned below:\\n\\n• 1601 transaction\\n• 2 errors\\n• August - 99.77%, September – 100%, October MTD – 99.81%\\n• Aug to Oct MTD, Quality score – 99.94%\\n\\nAdditionally, we have not charged clients for all the transactions that were processed in error (9 errors), waiving a total of $127.77 due to quality issues\\n\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Wright-Gardner Insurance - Output - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "WGIBGL", "Segment": "C", "Manager": "Naveen Raj", "Supervisor": "Naveen Raj", "Teamleader": "Naveen Raj", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Quality", "Issue Type": "Client reports multiple errors by the team or a processor", "Detailed Description": "Background: On July 17th, the client raised quality concerns with CE (Margery Schumick) during a phone call. Wright Gardner is a third-generation family business in a poor financial state. Previously reduced operations to 2 FTEs before transitioning to India. \\n\\nAfter Christian Wright escalated the issue of quality errors, and following the clarification questions, there has been a request to move the team back to China. \\n\\nClient reported 12 feedback and stated all were errors: \\nFindings: Total Feedback received 12, of which 4 are errors, and the remaining were clarifications. \\n\\n- 2 Procedure Issues (Audited by the China team). \\n- 1 Training and Understanding (followed the procedure)\\n- 1 Clerical Error\\n- 8 Clarifications\\n\\nBoth the procedure Issues and clarifications were caused by Special scenarios. The China team has acknowledged this and confirmed that they will be refined on Policy Checking, Post Production, and Cancellation tasks with the OpEx support. \\n\\nPerformance summary from Jan to July 2025: \\n3165 transactions | 7 errors | Quality Score: 99.78% | Utilization: 2.56\\n\\nIt is important to note:\\n- We were unable to establish an introductory call with the client, as meeting requests were not accepted.\\n- Our request to present the RCA and actions taken was declined by the client team.\\n- The clarifications raised were tied to unique cases, and the China team has acknowledged the need for procedure refinements in Policy Checking, Post Production, and Cancellation tasks, with OpEx support.\\n\\nActions Taken:\\n1. Processing is now handled exclusively by qualified trainers.\\n2. All questions directed to clients are first reviewed and routed through the China team to ensure alignment.\\n3. Procedure Reviews and update - Ongoing\\n\\n\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "Alignment on Transition Back to China \\n1. Brenda shared the transition-back progress. The China team has taken over all tasks within one month, except for Online Rating. \\n2. Bangalore team stops touching any new work immediately from Friday, 11/21. They will only complete their open cases (ex., pending follow ups, tasks that are under working, etc). China team will work with Bangalore team to get a clear cut off once they complete the open cases. \\n3. For Online Rating, client will take it back in-house temporarily, and the China team will start the training immediately. The China team will require cases from you for training carrier by carrier gradually until we ramp up for the full volume. \\n4. For post-production, the China team won’t be trained on this as it’s not a routine task anymore. \\n", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": "6-1(10/21/2025):The WGI client server has been online since September 10th, and the team has begun processing tasks. We have compiled backlog details from August 20th to September 10th, during which there are 234 pending volumes to address. We are continuously consolidating the backlog information and have shared it with clients (Cindy). \\nIn collaboration with BGL and CN, the CN team will manage all backlogged policy checks, while BGL will handle all other tasks.  \\n* On September 16, we provided a backlog clearance plan, estimating that it would take approximately 144 hours to clear the backlog by October 17. However, due to delays in receiving server access for the new CN team members, the deadline for clearing the backlog has been extended to October 31.\\n* The team has cleared all the backlog for all the tasks except Policy checking, and as aligned with the client, the outstanding backlog on policy checking will be cleared by 10/31.\\n\\n", "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Wright-Gardner Insurance - Output - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "WGIBGL", "Segment": "C", "Manager": "Naveen Raj", "Supervisor": "Naveen Raj", "Teamleader": "Naveen Raj", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "IT/Systems", "Issue Type": "Client system is down causing team unable to access the system for longer than a day", "Detailed Description": "Background:\\n\\n* On 08/20 after 3 PM IST the team was not able to connect to the server. The system issue was reported to clients (Cindy J. Sowers) on the same day along with CE (Margery Schumick).\\n* Client responded back stating they are still working to fix the issue and will keep us updated once the server is back online.\\n* on 08/21 again team was unable to connect to the server and it was raised to the client.\\n* On 08/22 received an email from client (Renee Brennan - Vice President of Commercial Operations) informing that the server will not be available until 08/27.\\n* Due to this system issue, we foresee that the account will not be meeting the monthly minimum billing of $6,850 for August 2025 and notified CE for further directions.\\n\\nResolution Process:\\n\\n* Once the system is back online, we will review the outstanding task and provide catch up plan with clients. \\n\\n\\n\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": "The issue has been unresolved for longer than 30 days. So it's automatically elevated to the upper level.", "Closed Reason": "System issue resolved and the team has cleared all the backlog for all the tasks except Policy checking, and as aligned with the client, the outstanding backlog on policy checking will be cleared by 10/31.", "Result of Resolution": "Improved Relationship", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"},
  {"Record(s)": null, "Parent Company": null, "Account Name": "Wright-Gardner Insurance - Output - Bangalore", "Abbreviation": "WGIBGL", "Segment": "C", "Manager": "Naveen Raj", "Supervisor": "Naveen Raj", "Teamleader": "Naveen Raj", "Client Executive": null, "Partnership Executive": null, "Category": "Pricing/Competitive Threat", "Issue Type": "Client expresses concern about pricing", "Detailed Description": "Background:\\nThe client has requested a reduction in 2026 rates or several months free for the errors made. On July 17th, during a call with Margery Schumick, the client raised concerns about the quality errors, and Christian Wright (Client team) requested the account to be moved back to China. \\n\\nRoot Cause:\\nErrors: Out of 12 feedback items, 4 were actual errors:\\n• 2 Procedure Issues (audited by the China team)\\n• 1 Training and Understanding Issue\\n• 1 Clerical Error\\nClarifications: 8 requests were clarifications, tied to special scenarios needing procedure refinements.\\nCommunication Gap: No introductory call as the client denied it and the RCA presentation request was declined by the client.\\n\\nPerformance Summary (Jan to July 2025):\\n• 3165 transactions\\n• 7 errors\\n• Quality Score: 99.78%\\n• Utilization: 2.56\\nAction Plan:\\n\\n• Qualified Trainers: Processing is now handled exclusively by qualified trainers.\\n• Client Communication: All client-directed questions are reviewed by the China team for alignment.\\n• Procedure Refinement: Ongoing reviews and updates in Policy Checking, Post Production, and Cancellation tasks with OpEx support.\\n• Account transfer to China - By the end of January 2026.    \\nQuality status after July 2025:\\n\\n• 1601 transaction\\n• 2 errors\\n• August - 99.77%, September – 100%, October MTD – 99.81%\\n• Aug to Oct MTD, Quality score – 99.94%\\n\\nAdditionally, we have not charged clients for all the transactions that were processed in error (9 errors), waiving a total of $127.77 due to quality issues\\n", "Status": "Closed", "Created Year": 2025, "Closed Year": 2025, "Reopen Year": null, "Color": "Red", "Color Change Reason": null, "Closed Reason": "We are closing the pricing/competitive issues based on advice from CE (Margery). The client’s concerns are not related to pricing or competitive threats. Instead, their concerns about “cost” or “pricing” arise from quality issues. Therefore, I will incorporate the pricing concerns into the quality CARE alert that was raised in July 2025.", "Result of Resolution": "Ongoing Actions", "Apply to Parent Company": null, "Shift": "Regular", "Director": "Rajesh Calambakam", "Location": "Bangalore"}
